# Database migrations

Schema changes are **Alembic-only**. Production and Docker boot run `flask db upgrade` via [`entrypoint.sh`](../entrypoint.sh) — not `migrations/legacy_sqlite/run_migrations.py`.

## Required workflow for every schema change

1. Update SQLAlchemy models in `models/`
2. `flask db revision --autogenerate -m "describe_change"` (or hand-write incremental revision)
3. Review `alembic_migrations/versions/` — confirm `down_revision` chains to current head
4. `flask db upgrade` locally
5. Extend `tests/test_migrations.py` and/or `tests/test_schema_parity.py`

## Do not

- Add executable DDL only under `migrations/legacy_sqlite/` — that directory is archived reference; boot will skip it
- Ship model columns without a matching Alembic revision in the same PR
- Assume `alembic stamp head` alone upgrades schema — it only records revision, no DDL

## Legacy transition

Existing SQLite DBs may have `schema_migrations` from the pre-Alembic runner. New Alembic revisions after the baseline must be **idempotent** when practical (`column_exists` in [`alembic_migrations/migration_helpers.py`](../alembic_migrations/migration_helpers.py)) so databases manually patched via legacy files still upgrade cleanly.

